al money is scheduled to be usable nationwide starting at the end of this year."},{"name":"~에서 (location/source)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"location. 전국 → 전국에서 = \\"throughout the country\\".","ex_ko":"이 새로운 디지털 돈은 올해 말부터 전국에서 사용할 수 있을 예정입니다.","ex_en":"This new digital money is scheduled to be usable nationwide starting at the end of this year."},{"name":"~부터 (from)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"starting from. 올해 말 → 올해 말부터 = \\"from the end of this year\\".","ex_ko":"이 새로운 디지털 돈은 올해 말부터 전국에서 사용할 수 있을 예정입니다.","ex_en":"This new digital money is scheduled to be usable nationwide starting at the end of this year."},{"name":"~(으)ㄹ 전망이다 / 계획이다 / 방침이다 / 예정이다 (is expected / planned to)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"formal future intent. 사용할 수 있다 → 사용할 수 있을 예정이다 = \\"is scheduled to be usable\\".","ex_ko":"이 새로운 디지털 돈은 올해 말부터 전국에서 사용할 수 있을 예정입니다.","ex_en":"This new digital money is scheduled to be usable nationwide starting at the end of this year."},{"name":"~고 있다 (continuous)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"progressive. 살다 → 살고 있다 → 살고 있습니다 = \\"are living\\".","ex_ko":"약 14억 명의 사람들이 살고 있습니다.","ex_en":"About 1.4 billion people live there."},{"name":"~(으)려고 (intention)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"intention. 만들다 → 만들려고 (하다) = \\"intends to make\\".","ex_ko":"정부는 디지털 화폐로 금융 서비스(돈을 저축하고 보내는 일)를 더 편리하게 만들려고 해요.","ex_en":"The government intends to make financial services (saving and sending money) more convenient with digital currency."},{"name":"~게 하다 (causative)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"periphrastic causative. 편리하다 → 편리하게 만들다 = \\"to make convenient\\". <stem> + 게 만들다/하다.","ex_ko":"정부는 디지털 화폐로 금융 서비스(돈을 저축하고 보내는 일)를 더 편리하게 만들려고 해요.","ex_en":"The government intends to make financial services (saving and sending money) more convenient with digital currency."},{"name":"~(으)로 (means/direction)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"means. 디지털 화폐 → 디지털 화폐로 = \\"with / by means of digital currency\\".","ex_ko":"정부는 디지털 화폐로 금융 서비스(돈을 저축하고 보내는 일)를 더 편리하게 만들려고 해요.","ex_en":"The government intends to make financial services (saving and sending money) more convenient with digital currency."},{"name":"~하고 (with/and, conv)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"conversational \\"and\\". 저축하다 → 저축하고 보내는 = \\"save and send\\".","ex_ko":"정부는 디지털 화폐로 금융 서비스(돈을 저축하고 보내는 일)를 더 편리하게 만들려고 해요.","ex_en":"The government intends to make financial services (saving and sending money) more convenient with digital currency."},{"name":"~과/와 (with/and)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"formal \\"and\\". 중국 → 중국과 유럽연합 = \\"China and the EU\\".","ex_ko":"중국과 유럽연합도 이미 디지털 화폐를 준비하고 있어요.","ex_en":"China and the European Union are also already preparing digital currencies."},{"name":"~(이)라고 하다 / ~(이)라고 밝히다 (indirect copula/name + news reporting)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"reported speech (identification). 될 것이다 → 될 것이라고 말합니다 = \\"says that (it) will become\\".","ex_ko":"전문가들은 디지털 화폐가 미래의 돈이 될 것이라고 말합니다.","ex_en":"Experts say that digital currency will be the money of the future."}]}') ON CONFLICT (article_id) DO UPDATE SET translation = EXCLUDED.translation, vocab = COALESCE(EXCLUDED.vocab, article_cache.vocab), grammar = COALESCE(EXCLUDED.grammar, article_cache.grammar);
INSERT INTO article_cache (article_id, translation, vocab, grammar) VALUES (E'moknthahfb0g', E'{"texts":["Japan Airlines (JAL) announced that starting next month, it will officially use humanoid robots at Haneda Airport. These robots are scheduled to handle ground operations at the airport.","The robots will end up taking on tasks such as passenger guidance and luggage handling. It plans to cooperate together with airport staff and provide better service.","Due to its aging society, Japan has a serious labor shortage problem. In the aviation industry too, robot technology is being actively used to address the manpower shortage.","Korea\'s Incheon International Airport is also reviewing similar robot services. Going forward, encountering robots at airports is expected to become more common."],"sentences":[{"text":"일본항공(JAL)이 다음 달부터 하네다 공항에서 인간형 로봇(humanoid robot)을 정식으로 사용한다고 발표했어요.","translation":"Japan Airlines (JAL) announced that starting next month, it will officially use humanoid robots at Haneda Airport.","vocab":[{"ko":"공항","en":"airport","note":""},{"ko":"인간형","en":"humanoid","note":""},{"ko":"정식","en":"official, formal","note":""},{"ko":"발표하다","en":"to announce","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"했어요 (하다 past polite)","exp":"하다 past polite. 발표하다 → 발표했어요 = \\"announced\\".","example_in_sentence":"발표했어요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~았/었/였어요 (past polite)","exp":"past polite. 하다 stems contract to 했-: 발표하다 → 발표했어요.","example_in_sentence":"발표했어요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~에서 (location/source)","exp":"location. 공항 → 공항에서 = \\"at the airport\\".","example_in_sentence":"공항에서"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~(으)로 (means/direction)","exp":"means / manner. 정식 → 정식으로 = \\"officially / in an official manner\\".","example_in_sentence":"정식으로"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~부터 (from)","exp":"starting from. 다음 달 → 다음 달부터 = \\"starting next month\\".","example_in_sentence":"다음 달부터"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~다고 하다 / ~다고 밝히다 / ~다고 강조하다 (indirect declarative + news reporting verbs)","exp":"reported speech (declarative). 사용하다 → 사용한다고 발표했어요 = \\"announced that (it) will use\\".","example_in_sentence":"사용한다고 발표했어요"}]},{"text":"이 로봇들은 공항 지상 업무를 담당할 예정입니다.","translation":"These robots are scheduled to handle ground operations at the airport.","vocab":[{"ko":"지상","en":"ground (level)","note":""},{"ko":"업무","en":"work, duties","note":""},{"ko":"담당하다","en":"to be in charge of","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~(으)ㄹ 전망이다 / 계획이다 / 방침이다 / 예정이다 (is expected / planned to)","exp":"formal news-register future intent. 담당하다 → 담당할 예정이다 = \\"is scheduled to handle\\".","example_in_sentence":"담당할 예정입니다"}]},{"text":"로봇들은 승객 안내와 짐 운반 등의 업무를 맡게 되어요.","translation":"The robots will end up taking on tasks such as passenger guidance and luggage handling.","vocab":[{"ko":"승객","en":"passenger","note":""},{"ko":"안내","en":"guidance","note":""},{"ko":"짐","en":"luggage","note":""},{"ko":"운반","en":"transport, carrying","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~게 되다 (come to / passive)","exp":"circumstantial change. 맡다 → 맡게 되다 → 맡게 되어요 = \\"comes to take on / ends up handling\\".","example_in_sentence":"맡게 되어요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~과/와 (with/and)","exp":"formal \\"and\\". 안내 → 안내와 짐 운반 = \\"guidance and luggage handling\\".","example_in_sentence":"안내와 짐 운반"},{"type":"expression","label":"~ 등(의)","exp":"\\"~ etc. / and so on\\". 업무 → 업무를 = listed multiple followed by 등 = \\"such as ~ etc.\\".","example_in_sentence":"등의 업무"}]},{"text":"공항 직원들과 함께 협력하여 더 나은 서비스를 제공할 계획입니다.","translation":"It plans to cooperate together with airport staff and provide better service.","vocab":[{"ko":"직원","en":"staff, employee","note":""},{"ko":"협력하다","en":"to cooperate","note":""},{"ko":"낫다","en":"to be better","note":"ㅅ-irregular: 낫+은 → 나은"},{"ko":"제공하다","en":"to provide","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~께(서) (honorific dative/subject)","exp":"honorific marker for elders / superiors. (Regex false-positive on 함께 here.)","example_in_sentence":""},{"type":"grammar","label":"~과/와 (with/and)","exp":"formal \\"with\\". 직원들 → 직원들과 함께 = \\"together with the staff\\".","example_in_sentence":"직원들과 함께"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~(으)ㄹ 전망이다 / 계획이다 / 방침이다 / 예정이다 (is expected / planned to)","exp":"formal future intent. 제공하다 → 제공할 계획이다 = \\"plans to provide\\".","example_in_sentence":"제공할 계획입니다"},{"type":"expression","label":"~여/하여 (formal connector)","exp":"formal connective form of ~아/어서. 협력하다 → 협력하여 = \\"by cooperating / and cooperate\\".","example_in_sentence":"협력하여"}]},{"text":"일본은 고령화 사회로 인해 노동력 부족 문제가 심각해요.","translation":"Due to its aging society, Japan has a serious labor shortage problem.","vocab":[{"ko":"고령화","en":"aging (of population)","note":""},{"ko":"노동력","en":"workforce, labor force","note":""},{"ko":"부족","en":"shortage","note":""},{"ko":"심각하다","en":"to be serious","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~(으)로 (means/direction)","exp":"means / cause marker. 사회 → 사회로 = \\"as a society / by means of\\".","example_in_sentence":"사회로"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~(으)로 인해/인한 (due to)","exp":"causation. 고령화 사회 → 고령화 사회로 인해 = \\"due to the aging society\\".","example_in_sentence":"고령화 사회로 인해"}]},{"text":"항공업계에서도 인력난을 해결하기 위해 로봇 기술을 적극 활용하고 있습니다.","translation":"In the aviation industry too, robot technology is being actively used to address the manpower shortage.","vocab":[{"ko":"업계","en":"industry","note":""},{"ko":"인력난","en":"manpower shortage","note":""},{"ko":"해결하다","en":"to solve","note":""},{"ko":"활용하다","en":"to utilize","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~고 있다 (continuous)","exp":"progressive. 활용하다 → 활용하고 있다 = \\"is utilizing\\".","example_in_sentence":"활용하고 있습니다"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~기 위해(서) (in order to)","exp":"purpose. 해결하다 → 해결하기 위해 = \\"in order to solve\\".","example_in_sentence":"해결하기 위해"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~하고 (with/and, conv)","exp":"conversational \\"and\\". (Regex hit on the 하고 in 활용하고.)","example_in_sentence":""},{"type":"grammar","label":"~도 (also)","exp":"inclusive. 항공업계에서 → 항공업계에서도 = \\"in the aviation industry, too\\".","example_in_sentence":"항공업계에서도"}]},{"text":"한국의 인천국제공항도 비슷한 로봇 서비스를 검토하고 있어요.","translation":"Korea\'s Incheon International Airport is also reviewing similar robot services.","vocab":[{"ko":"비슷하다","en":"to be similar","note":""},{"ko":"검토하다","en":"to review, examine","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~고 있다 (continuous)","exp":"progressive. 검토하다 → 검토하고 있다 = \\"is reviewing\\".","example_in_sentence":"검토하고 있어요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~하고 (with/and, conv)","exp":"conversational \\"and\\". (Regex hit on 하고 in 검토하고.)","example_in_sentence":""},{"type":"grammar","label":"~도 (also)","exp":"inclusive. 인천국제공항 → 인천국제공항도 = \\"Incheon Airport, too\\".","example_in_sentence":"인천국제공항도"}]},{"text":"앞으로 공항에서 로봇을 만나는 일이 더 흔해질 것으로 보입니다.","translation":"Going forward, encountering robots at airports is expected to become more common.","vocab":[{"ko":"앞으로","en":"from now on, going forward","note":""},{"ko":"만나다","en":"to meet, encounter","note":""},{"ko":"흔하다","en":"to be common","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~에서 (location/source)","exp":"location. 공항 → 공항에서 = \\"at the airport\\".","example_in_sentence":"공항에서"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~(으)로 (means/direction)","exp":"means/quotative. 흔해질 것 → 흔해질 것으로 보이다 = \\"appears that (it) will become common\\".","example_in_sentence":"흔해질 것으로"},{"type":"expression","label":"~(으)로 보이다","exp":"\\"appears that / is seen as\\". <clause>+(으)로 보이다 = \\"is expected / appears\\".","example_in_sentence":"것으로 보입니다"},{"type":"expression","label":"~아/어지다 (become)","exp":"change-of-state. 흔하다 → 흔해지다 → 흔해질 = \\"will become common\\".","example_in_sentence":"흔해질"}]}],"version":"s5"}', E'[{"ko":"공항","en":"airport","note":""},{"ko":"인간형","en":"humanoid","note":""},{"ko":"정식","en":"official, formal","note":""},{"ko":"발표하다","en":"to announce","note":""},{"ko":"지상","en":"ground (level)","note":""},{"ko":"업무","en":"work, du