으)로 (means/direction)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"means/quotative. 흔해질 것 → 흔해질 것으로 보이다 = \\"appears that (it) will become common\\".","ex_ko":"일본항공(JAL)이 다음 달부터 하네다 공항에서 인간형 로봇(humanoid robot)을 정식으로 사용한다고 발표했어요.","ex_en":"Japan Airlines (JAL) announced that starting next month, it will officially use humanoid robots at Haneda Airport."},{"name":"~부터 (from)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"starting from. 다음 달 → 다음 달부터 = \\"starting next month\\".","ex_ko":"일본항공(JAL)이 다음 달부터 하네다 공항에서 인간형 로봇(humanoid robot)을 정식으로 사용한다고 발표했어요.","ex_en":"Japan Airlines (JAL) announced that starting next month, it will officially use humanoid robots at Haneda Airport."},{"name":"~다고 하다 / ~다고 밝히다 / ~다고 강조하다 (indirect declarative + news reporting verbs)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"reported speech (declarative). 사용하다 → 사용한다고 발표했어요 = \\"announced that (it) will use\\".","ex_ko":"일본항공(JAL)이 다음 달부터 하네다 공항에서 인간형 로봇(humanoid robot)을 정식으로 사용한다고 발표했어요.","ex_en":"Japan Airlines (JAL) announced that starting next month, it will officially use humanoid robots at Haneda Airport."},{"name":"~(으)ㄹ 전망이다 / 계획이다 / 방침이다 / 예정이다 (is expected / planned to)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"formal news-register future intent. 담당하다 → 담당할 예정이다 = \\"is scheduled to handle\\".","ex_ko":"이 로봇들은 공항 지상 업무를 담당할 예정입니다.","ex_en":"These robots are scheduled to handle ground operations at the airport."},{"name":"~게 되다 (come to / passive)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"circumstantial change. 맡다 → 맡게 되다 → 맡게 되어요 = \\"comes to take on / ends up handling\\".","ex_ko":"로봇들은 승객 안내와 짐 운반 등의 업무를 맡게 되어요.","ex_en":"The robots will end up taking on tasks such as passenger guidance and luggage handling."},{"name":"~과/와 (with/and)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"formal \\"and\\". 안내 → 안내와 짐 운반 = \\"guidance and luggage handling\\".","ex_ko":"로봇들은 승객 안내와 짐 운반 등의 업무를 맡게 되어요.","ex_en":"The robots will end up taking on tasks such as passenger guidance and luggage handling."},{"name":"~께(서) (honorific dative/subject)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"honorific marker for elders / superiors. (Regex false-positive on 함께 here.)","ex_ko":"공항 직원들과 함께 협력하여 더 나은 서비스를 제공할 계획입니다.","ex_en":"It plans to cooperate together with airport staff and provide better service."},{"name":"~(으)로 인해/인한 (due to)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"causation. 고령화 사회 → 고령화 사회로 인해 = \\"due to the aging society\\".","ex_ko":"일본은 고령화 사회로 인해 노동력 부족 문제가 심각해요.","ex_en":"Due to its aging society, Japan has a serious labor shortage problem."},{"name":"~고 있다 (continuous)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"progressive. 활용하다 → 활용하고 있다 = \\"is utilizing\\".","ex_ko":"항공업계에서도 인력난을 해결하기 위해 로봇 기술을 적극 활용하고 있습니다.","ex_en":"In the aviation industry too, robot technology is being actively used to address the manpower shortage."},{"name":"~기 위해(서) (in order to)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"purpose. 해결하다 → 해결하기 위해 = \\"in order to solve\\".","ex_ko":"항공업계에서도 인력난을 해결하기 위해 로봇 기술을 적극 활용하고 있습니다.","ex_en":"In the aviation industry too, robot technology is being actively used to address the manpower shortage."},{"name":"~하고 (with/and, conv)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"conversational \\"and\\". (Regex hit on the 하고 in 활용하고.)","ex_ko":"항공업계에서도 인력난을 해결하기 위해 로봇 기술을 적극 활용하고 있습니다.","ex_en":"In the aviation industry too, robot technology is being actively used to address the manpower shortage."},{"name":"~도 (also)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"inclusive. 항공업계에서 → 항공업계에서도 = \\"in the aviation industry, too\\".","ex_ko":"항공업계에서도 인력난을 해결하기 위해 로봇 기술을 적극 활용하고 있습니다.","ex_en":"In the aviation industry too, robot technology is being actively used to address the manpower shortage."}]}') ON CONFLICT (article_id) DO UPDATE SET translation = EXCLUDED.translation, vocab = COALESCE(EXCLUDED.vocab, article_cache.vocab), grammar = COALESCE(EXCLUDED.grammar, article_cache.grammar);
INSERT INTO article_cache (article_id, translation, vocab, grammar) VALUES (E'monnobjxw88m', E'{"texts":["A person rescued a small bird. The bird was injured or in a dangerous situation.","After (the bird) was rescued, a surprising thing happened. The small bird does not want to leave the hand of the person who rescued it.","The bird keeps sitting on top of that person\'s hand. It seems as if (it) is expressing a feeling of gratitude.","This kind of scene is very special and moving. It shows that animals also remember a person\'s help and feel grateful."],"sentences":[{"text":"한 사람이 작은 새 한 마리를 구해주었어요.","translation":"A person rescued a small bird.","vocab":[{"ko":"구하다","en":"to save, rescue","note":""},{"ko":"마리","en":"counter for animals","note":"새 한 마리 = one bird"}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~았/었/였어요 (past polite)","exp":"past polite ending. 주다 → 주었어요 = \\"gave / did (for someone)\\". Vowel harmony: ㅏ/ㅗ → 았; else → 었.","example_in_sentence":"구해주었어요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~아/어/여요 (present polite)","exp":"present polite informal ending. (Past form 주었어요 ends with 요 as well.)","example_in_sentence":""},{"type":"grammar","label":"~아/어 주다 (do for)","exp":"do as a favor. 구하다 → 구해 주다 → 구해주었어요 = \\"saved (for him/it)\\".","example_in_sentence":"구해주었어요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~ㄴ/은 (past verb / present adj modifier)","exp":"adjective present modifier. 작다 → 작은 새 = \\"small bird\\".","example_in_sentence":"작은 새"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~을/를 (object marker)","exp":"direct object particle. 새 한 마리 → 새 한 마리를 = \\"(rescued) a bird\\".","example_in_sentence":"새 한 마리를"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~이/가 (subject marker)","exp":"subject particle. 사람 → 사람이 = \\"a person (subject)\\".","example_in_sentence":"한 사람이"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~은/는 (topic marker)","exp":"topic particle. (Not in this sentence; regex hit on 한 or 손 etc. — treat as catalog reference.)","example_in_sentence":""}]},{"text":"새는 다쳤거나 위험한 상황에 있었어요.","translation":"The bird was injured or in a dangerous situation.","vocab":[{"ko":"다치다","en":"to get hurt, injured","note":""},{"ko":"위험하다","en":"to be dangerous","note":""},{"ko":"상황","en":"situation","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~았/었/였어요 (past polite)","exp":"past polite. 있다 → 있었어요 = \\"was / existed\\". 다치다 → 다쳤다 = \\"got hurt\\".","example_in_sentence":"있었어요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~아/어/여요 (present polite)","exp":"present polite ending pattern (here in past form 있었어요).","example_in_sentence":""},{"type":"grammar","label":"~거나 (or)","exp":"alternative connector. 다치다 → 다쳤거나 = \\"was hurt or ~\\". <stem> + 거나 = \\"or\\".","example_in_sentence":"다쳤거나"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~(이)나 (or / about / as much as)","exp":"alternation particle. (Regex hit on 거나; the (이)나 noun particle is not in this sentence.)","example_in_sentence":""},{"type":"grammar","label":"~은/는 (topic marker)","exp":"topic particle. 새 → 새는 = \\"the bird (as for the bird)\\".","example_in_sentence":"새는"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~에 (location/time)","exp":"static location. 상황 → 상황에 = \\"in (the) situation\\".","example_in_sentence":"상황에"}]},{"text":"새를 구해준 후에 놀라운 일이 일어났어요.","translation":"After (the bird) was rescued, a surprising thing happened.","vocab":[{"ko":"놀랍다","en":"to be surprising","note":"ㅂ-irregular: 놀랍+은 → 놀라운"},{"ko":"일어나다","en":"to happen, occur","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~았/었/였어요 (past polite)","exp":"past polite. 일어나다 → 일어났어요 = \\"happened\\". Stem vowel ㅏ + 았 → 났.","example_in_sentence":"일어났어요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~아/어/여요 (present polite)","exp":"present polite ending pattern (here as past 났어요).","example_in_sentence":""},{"type":"grammar","label":"~을/를 (object marker)","exp":"direct object particle. 새 → 새를 = \\"(rescued) the bird\\".","example_in_sentence":"새를"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~이/가 (subject marker)","exp":"subject particle. 일 → 일이 = \\"a thing (subject)\\".","example_in_sentence":"놀라운 일이"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~에 (location/time)","exp":"time marker. 후 → 후에 = \\"after\\".","example_in_sentence":"후에"},{"type":"expression","label":"~ㄴ/은 후에 (after V-ing)","exp":"time sequence. 구해주다 → 구해준 후에 = \\"after rescuing\\". <past modifier> + 후에 = \\"after V-ing\\".","example_in_sentence":"구해준 후에"}]},{"text":"작은 새가 구해준 사람의 손을 떠나려고 하지 않아요.","translation":"The small bird does not want to leave the hand of the person who rescued it.","vocab":[{"ko":"손","en":"hand","note":""},{"ko":"떠나다","en":"to leave","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~지 않다","exp":"long-form negation. 떠나려고 하다 → 떠나려고 하지 않다 = \\"does not try to leave\\". <stem> + 지 않다.","example_in_sentence":"하지 않아요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~아/어/여요 (present polite)","exp":"present polite ending. 않다 → 않아요 = \\"does not\\".","example_in_sentence":"않아요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~지요/~죠 (confirming)","exp":"seeking agreement. (Here regex false-positive on 하지; the confirming ~지요 is not used.)","example_in_sentence":""},{"type":"grammar","label":"~(으)려고 (intention)","exp":"intention. 떠나다 → 떠나려고 (하다) = \\"intending to leave / trying to leave\\".","example_in_sentence":"떠나려고"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~ㄴ/은 (past verb / present adj modifier)","exp":"verb past modifier. 구해주다 → 구해준 사람 = \\"the person who rescued (it)\\". 작다 → 작은 새 = \\"small bird\\".","example_in_sentence":"구해준 사람"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~을/를 (object marker)","exp":"direct object particle. 손 → 손을 = \\"(does not leave) the hand\\".","example_in_sentence":"손을"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~이/가 (subject marker)","exp":"subject particle. 새 → 새가 = \\"the bird (subject)\\".","example_in_sentence":"새가"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~은/는 (topic marker)","exp":"topic particle. (Regex hit; the topic marker is implicit here.)","example_in_sentence":""},{"type":"grammar","label":"~의 (possessive)","exp":"possessive / attributive","example_in_sentence":"사람의"}]},{"text":"새는 그 사람의 손 위에 계속 앉아 있어요.","translation":"The bird keeps sitting on top of that person\'s hand.","vocab":[{"ko":"위","en":"top, above","note":""},{"ko":"계속","en":"continuously","note":""},{"ko":"앉다","en":"to sit","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~아/어/여요 (present polite)","exp":"present polite. 있다 → 있어요 = \\"is\\".","example_in_sentence":"있어요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~아/어 있다 (resultant state)","exp":"resultant state. 앉다 → 앉아 있다 = \\"is sitting (and remains seated)\\".","example_in_sentence":"앉아 있어요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~은/는 (topic marker)","exp":"topic particle. 새 → 새는 = \\"as for the bird\\".","example_in_sentence":"새는"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~에 (location/time)","exp":"location. 위 → 위에 = \\"on top of\\".","example_in_sentence":"손 위에"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~의 (possessive)","exp":"possessive. 사람 → 사람의 손 = \\"the person\'s hand\\".","example_in_sentence":"사람의 손"}]},{"text":"마치 고마운 마음을 표현하는 것 같아요.","translation":"It seems as if (it) is expressing a feeling of gratitude.","vocab":[{"ko":"고맙다","en":"to be thankful","note":"ㅂ-irregular: 고맙+은 → 고마운"},{"ko":"마음","en":"heart, mind","note":""},{"ko":"표현하다","en":"to express","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~아/어/여요 (present polite)","exp":"present polite. 같다 → 같아요 = \\"seems / is like\\".","example_in_sentence":"같아요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~는 (present verb modifier)","exp":"present verb modifier. 표현하다 → 표현하는 것 = \\"the thing of expressing\\".","example_in_sentence":"표현하는 것"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~을/를 (object marker)","exp":"direct object. 마음 → 마음을 = \\"(expressing) the feeling\\".","example_in_sentence":"마음을"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~은/는 (topic marker)","exp":"topic particle. (Implicit; regex hit on 는 inside 는 것.)","example_in_sentence":""},{"type":"grammar","label":"~는 것 (the thing of V-ing)","exp":"verbal nominalizer. 표현하다 → 표현하는 것 = \\"the act of expressing\\".","example_in_sentence":"표현하는 것"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~ㄴ/는/을 것 같다 (seems)","exp":"conjecture. 표현하는 것 같다 = \\"seems to be expressing\\".","example_in_sentence":"표현하는 것 같아요"},{"type":"expression","label":"마치 ~ 같다","exp":"\\"as if / just like\\". 마치 ~ 것 같다 = \\"as if it were ~\\".","example_in_sentence":"마치 ~ 것 같아요"}]},{"text":"이런 모습은 매우 특별하고 감동적이에요.","translation":"This kind of scene is very special and moving.","vocab":[{"ko":"모습","en":"appearance, scene","note":""},{"ko":"특별하다","en":"to be special","note":""},{"ko":"감동적","en":"moving, touching","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~ㄴ/은 (past verb / present adj modifier)","exp":"adjective modifier. 이렇다 → 이런 모습 = \\"this kind of scene\\".","example_in_sentence":"이런 모습"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~적 (-ic / -al adjective suffix)","exp":"Sino-Korean noun → adjective. 감동 → 감동적 = \\"moving, touching\\".","example_in_sentence":"감동적이에요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~은/는 (topic marker)","exp":"topic particle. 모습 → 모습은 = \\"as for the scene\\".","example_in_sentence":"모습은"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~하고 (with/and, conv)","exp":"conversational connector. 특별하다 → 특별하고 = \\"is special, and ~\\".","example_in_sentence":"특별하고"}]},{"text":"동물도 사람의 도움을 기억하고 고마워한다는 걸 보여줘요.","translation":"It shows that animals also remember a person\'s help and feel grateful.","vocab":[{"ko":"동물","en":"animal","note":""},{"ko":"도움","en":"help","note":""},{"ko":"기억하다","en":"to remember","note":""},{"ko":"고마워하다","en":"to feel thankful","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~을/를 (object marker)","exp":"direct object. 도움 → 도움을 = \\"(remember) the help\\".","example_in_sentence":"도움을"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~은/는 (topic marker)","exp":"topic particle. (Regex hit on 는다는; topic ~은/는 is not separate here.)","example_in_sentence":""},{"type":"grammar","label":"~하고 (with/and, conv)","exp":"connector \\"and\\". 기억하다 → 기억하고 = \\"remembers, and ~\\".","example_in_sentence":"기억하고"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~도 (also)","exp":"inclusive. 동물 → 동물도 = \\"animals, too\\".","example_in_sentence":"동물도"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~의 (possessive)","exp":"possessive. 사람 → 사람의 도움 = \\"a person\'s help\\".","example_in_sentence":"사람의 도움"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~ㄴ/는다는 / ~라는 + N (the claim/fact/idea that)","exp":"attributive of reported clause. 고마워한다 → 고마워한다는 걸 = \\"the fact that (it) is grateful\\". <quote> + ㄴ/는다는 + 것.","example_in_sentence":"고마워한다는 걸"}]}],"version":"s5"}', E'[{"ko":"구하다","en":"to save, rescue","note":""},{"ko":"마리","en":"counter for animals","note":"새 한 마리 = one bird"},{"ko":"다치다","en":"to get hurt, injured","note":""},{"ko":"위험하다","en":"to be dangerous","note":""},{"ko":"상황","en":"situation","note":""},{"ko":"놀랍다","en":"to be surprising","note":"ㅂ-irregular: 놀랍+은 → 놀라운"},{"ko":"일어나다","en":"to happen, occur","note":""},{"ko":"손","en":"hand","note":""},{"ko":"떠나다","en":"to leave","note":""},{"ko":"위","en":"top, above","note":""},{"ko":"계속","en":"continuously","note":""},{"ko":"앉다","en":"to sit","note":""},{"ko":"고맙다","en":"to be thankful","note":"ㅂ-irregular: 고맙+은 → 고마운"},{"ko":"마음","en":"heart, mind","note":""},{"ko":"표현하다","en":"to express","note":""},{"ko":"모습","en":"appearance, scene","note":""},{"ko":"특별하다","en":"to be special","note":""},{"ko":"감동적","en":"moving, touching","note":""},{"ko":"동물","en":"animal","note":""},{"ko":"도움","en":"help","note":""},{"ko":"기억하다","en":"to remember","note":""},{"ko":"고마워하다","en":"to feel thankful","note":""}]', E'{"patterns":[{"name":"~았/었/였어요 (past polite)","level":"Starter","exp":"past polite ending. 주다 → 주었어요 = \\"gave / did (for someone)\\". Vowel harmony: ㅏ/ㅗ → 았; else → 었.","ex_ko":"한 사람이 작은 새 한 마리를 구해주었어요.","ex_en":"A person rescued a small bird."},{"name":"~아/어/여요 (present polite)","level":"Starter","exp":"present polite informal ending. (Past form 주었어요 ends with 요 as well.)","ex_ko":"한 사람이 작은 새 한 마리를 구해주었어요.","ex_en":"A person rescued a small bird."},{"name":"~아/어 주다 (do for)","level":"Starter","exp":"do as a favor. 구하다 → 구해 주다 → 구해주었어요 = \\"saved (for him/it)\\".","ex_ko":"한 사람이 작은 새 한 마리를 구해주었어요.","ex_en":"A person rescued a small bird."},{"name":"~ㄴ/은 (past verb / present adj modifier)","level":"Starter","exp":"verb past modifier. 구해주다 → 구해준 사람 = \\"the person who rescued (it)\\". 작다 → 작은 새 = \\"small bird\\".","ex_ko":"한 사람이 작은 새 한 마리를 구해주었어요.","ex_en":"A person rescued a small bird."},{"name":"~을/를 (object marker)","level":"Starter","exp":"direct object particle. 새 한 마리 → 새 한 마리를 = \\"(rescued) a bird\\".","ex_ko":"한 사람이 작은 새 한 마리를 구해주었어요.","ex_en":"A person rescued a small bird."},{"name":"~이/가 (subject marker)","level":"Starter","exp":"subject particle. 사람 → 사람이 = \\"a person (subject)\\".","ex_ko":"한 사람이 작은 새 한 마리를 구해주었어요.","ex_en":"A person rescued a small bird."},{"name":"~은/는 (topic marker)","level":"Starter","exp":"topic particle. (Not in this sentence; regex hit on 한 or 손 etc. — treat as catalog reference.)","ex_ko":"한 사람이 작은 새 한 마리를 구해주었어요.","ex_en":"A person rescued a small bird."},{"name":"~거나 (or)","level":"Starter","exp":"alternative connector. 다치다 → 다쳤거나 = \\"was hurt or ~\\". <stem> + 거나 = \\"or\\".","ex_ko":"새는 다쳤거나 위험한 상황에 있었어요.","ex_en":"The bird was injured or in a dangerous situation."},{"name":"~(이)나 (or / about / as much as)","level":"Starter","exp":"alternation particle. (Regex hit on 거나; the (이)나 noun particle is not in this sentence.)","ex_ko":"새는 다쳤거나 위험한 상황에 있었어요.","ex_en":"The bird was injured or in a dangerous situation."},{"name":"~에 (location/time)","level":"Starter","exp":"static location. 상황 → 상황에 = \\"in (the) situation\\".","ex_ko":"새는 다쳤거나 위험한 상황에 있었어요.","ex_en":"The bird was injured or in a dangerous situation."},{"name":"~지 않다","level":"Starter","exp":"long-form negation. 떠나려고 하다 → 떠나려고 하지 않다 = \\"does not try to leave\\". <stem> + 지 않다.","ex_ko":"작은 새가 구해준 사람의 손을 떠나려고 하지 않아요.","ex_en":"The small bird does not want to leave the hand of the person who rescued it."},{"name":"~지요/~죠 (confirming)","level":"Starter","exp":"seeking agreement. (Here regex false-positive on 하지; the confirming ~지요 is not used.)","ex_ko":"작은 새가 구해준 사람의 손을 떠나려고 하지 않아요.","ex_en":"The small bird does not want to leave the hand of the person who rescued it."},{"name":"~(으)려고 (intention)","level":"Starter","exp":"intention. 떠나다 → 떠나려고 (하다) = \\"intending to leave / trying to leave\\".","ex_ko":"작은 새가 구해준 사람의 손을 떠나려고 하지 않아요.","ex_en":"The small bird does not want to leave the hand of the person who rescued it."},{"name":"~의 (possessive)","level":"Starter","exp":"possessive. 사람 → 사람의 손 = \\"the person\'s hand\\".","ex_ko":"작은 새가 구해준 사람의 손을 떠나려고 하지 않아요.","ex_en":"The small bird does not want to leave the hand of the person who rescued it."},{"name":"~아/어 있다 (resultant state)","level":"Starter","exp":"resultant state. 앉다 → 앉아 있다 = \\"is sitting (and remains seated)\\".","ex_ko":"새는 그 사람의 손 위에 계속 앉아 있어요.","ex_en":"The bird keeps sitting on top of that person\'s hand."}]}') ON CONFLICT (article_id) DO UPDATE SET translation = EXCLUDED.translation, vocab = COALESCE(EXCLUDED.vocab, article_cache.vocab), grammar = COALESCE(EXCLUDED.grammar, article_cache.grammar);
INSERT INTO article_cache (article_id, translation, vocab, grammar) VALUES (E'mortm5de1mh0', E'{"texts":["In one building in Bakersfield, California, 23 fires broke out over the course of a year. This building is an old building with historical value.","This kind of thing is not happening only in this building. Other historical buildings in the Bakersfield area are also burning one by one. Experts say that this might not be a coincidence.","Local residents are very worried about this situation. The fire department (the place that puts out fires) is investigating the cause of the fire. The police also joined the investigation.","When historical buildings disappear, the culture and history of that area also vanish along with them. In Korea too, protecting old buildings is an important issue. It is a situation that requires measures to prevent fires like these."],"sentences":[{"text":"미국 캘리포니아주 베이커즈필드의 한 건물에서 1년 동안 23번의 화재가 발생했어요.","translation":"In one building in Bakersfield, California, 23 fires broke out over the course of a year.","vocab":[{"ko":"건물","en":"building","note":""},{"ko":"화재","en":"fire (incident)","note":""},{"ko":"발생하다","en":"to occur, break out","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"했어요 (하다 past polite)","exp":"하다 verb past polite. 발생하다 → 발생했어요 = \\"occurred\\". 하다 stems contract to 했-.","example_in_sentence":"발생했어요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~았/었/였어요 (past polite)","exp":"past polite ending. 하다 stems take the 였- form which contracts to 했-: 발생하다 → 발생했어요.","example_in_sentence":"발생했어요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~에서 (location/source)","exp":"location where an action takes place. 건물 → 건물에서 = \\"in/at the building\\".","example_in_sentence":"건물에서"},{"type":"expression","label":"~ 동안","exp":"\\"during / for (a period)\\". 1년 → 1년 동안 = \\"for a year / over a year\\".","example_in_sentence":"1년 동안"}]},{"text":"이 건물은 역사적 가치가 있는 오래된 건물이에요.","translation":"This building is an old building with historical value.","vocab":[{"ko":"역사적","en":"historical","note":""},{"ko":"가치","en":"value","note":""},{"ko":"오래되다","en":"to be old (of objects)","note":"oft. attributive 오래된"}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~적 (-ic / -al adjective suffix)","exp":"Sino-Korean noun → adjective. 역사 → 역사적 = \\"historical\\".","example_in_sentence":"역사적 가치"}]},{"text":"이런 일이 이 건물에서만 일어나는 것이 아니에요.","translation":"This kind of thing is not happening only in this building.","vocab":[{"ko":"일어나다","en":"to happen, occur","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~만 (only)","exp":"limiter \\"only / just\\". 건물에서 → 건물에서만 = \\"only at the building\\".","example_in_sentence":"건물에서만"},{"type":"grammar","label":"ㄹ 탈락 (ㄹ drops before ㄴ/ㅅ/ㅂ)","exp":"ㄹ-deletion: stem-final ㄹ drops before ㄴ/ㅅ/ㅂ. 살다 → 사니/사세요, 만들다 → 만드세요.","example_in_sentence":""}]},{"text":"베이커즈필드 지역의 다른 역사적인 건물들도 하나씩 불타고 있어요.","translation":"Other historical buildings in the Bakersfield area are also burning one by one.","vocab":[{"ko":"지역","en":"area, region","note":""},{"ko":"불타다","en":"to burn (catch fire)","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~고 있다 (continuous)","exp":"progressive aspect. 불타다 → 불타고 있다 = \\"is burning\\".","example_in_sentence":"불타고 있어요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~적 (-ic / -al adjective suffix)","exp":"역사 → 역사적인 = \\"historical (modifier form)\\".","example_in_sentence":"역사적인 건물들"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~씩 (each / per)","exp":"distributive. 하나 → 하나씩 = \\"one by one / one each\\".","example_in_sentence":"하나씩"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~도 (also)","exp":"inclusive \\"also / too\\". 건물들 → 건물들도 = \\"buildings, too\\".","example_in_sentence":"건물들도"}]},{"text":"전문가들은 이것이 우연이 아닐 수도 있다고 말해요.","translation":"Experts say that this might not be a coincidence.","vocab":[{"ko":"전문가","en":"expert","note":""},{"ko":"우연","en":"coincidence, chance","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~도 (also)","exp":"inclusive. 수도 = 수 + 도 → \\"possibility, too / might also\\". 아닐 수도 있다 = \\"might not be\\".","example_in_sentence":"아닐 수도"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~다고 하다 / ~다고 밝히다 / ~다고 강조하다 (indirect declarative + news reporting verbs)","exp":"reported speech. <quote> + 다고 말하다 = \\"say that ~\\". 있다고 말해요 = \\"says that there is / might be\\".","example_in_sentence":"있다고 말해요"},{"type":"expression","label":"~(으)ㄹ 수도 있다","exp":"\\"might / may possibly\\". 아니다 → 아닐 수도 있다 = \\"might not be\\".","example_in_sentence":"아닐 수도 있다"}]},{"text":"지역 주민들은 이 상황을 매우 걱정하고 있어요.","translation":"Local residents are very worried about this situation.","vocab":[{"ko":"주민","en":"resident","note":""},{"ko":"상황","en":"situation","note":""},{"ko":"걱정하다","en":"to worry","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~고 있다 (continuous)","exp":"progressive aspect. 걱정하다 → 걱정하고 있다 = \\"is worrying / is worried\\".","example_in_sentence":"걱정하고 있어요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~하고 (with/and, conv)","exp":"conversational \\"with / and\\". (Here triggered by the ~하고 ending of 걱정하고 — the connector form, not the particle.)","example_in_sentence":""}]},{"text":"소방서(불을 끄는 일을 하는 곳)는 화재 원인을 조사하고 있어요.","translation":"The fire department (the place that puts out fires) is investigating the cause of the fire.","vocab":[{"ko":"소방서","en":"fire station","note":""},{"ko":"끄다","en":"to put out, turn off","note":"으-irregular: 끄+어 → 꺼"},{"ko":"원인","en":"cause","note":""},{"ko":"조사하다","en":"to investigate","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~고 있다 (continuous)","exp":"progressive aspect. 조사하다 → 조사하고 있다 = \\"is investigating\\".","example_in_sentence":"조사하고 있어요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~하고 (with/and, conv)","exp":"conversational \\"with / and\\". (Here triggered by 조사하고 — the connector form.)","example_in_sentence":""}]},{"text":"경찰도 함께 수사에 나섰어요.","translation":"The police also joined the investigation.","vocab":[{"ko":"경찰","en":"police","note":""},{"ko":"수사","en":"investigation (criminal)","note":""},{"ko":"나서다","en":"to step forward, take part","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~았/었/였어요 (past polite)","exp":"past polite. 나서다 → 나섰어요 = \\"stepped forward / joined\\". Stem 나서- + 었 + 어요.","example_in_sentence":"나섰어요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~께(서) (honorific dative/subject)","exp":"honorific marker for elders / superiors. 할아버지 → 할아버지께서. (Here regex false-positive on 함께; the particle is not actually present.)","example_in_sentence":""},{"type":"grammar","label":"~도 (also)","exp":"inclusive. 경찰 → 경찰도 = \\"the police, too\\".","example_in_sentence":"경찰도"},{"type":"expression","label":"함께","exp":"\\"together / along with\\". 경찰도 함께 = \\"the police also (joined) together\\".","example_in_sentence":"함께"}]},{"text":"역사적인 건물들이 사라지면 그 지역의 문화와 역사도 함께 없어져요.","translation":"When historical buildings disappear, the culture and history of that area also vanish along with them.","vocab":[{"ko":"사라지다","en":"to disappear","note":""},{"ko":"문화","en":"culture","note":""},{"ko":"없어지다","en":"to vanish, be gone","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~(으)면 (if/when)","exp":"conditional. 사라지다 → 사라지면 = \\"if / when (they) disappear\\".","example_in_sentence":"사라지면"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~적 (-ic / -al adjective suffix)","exp":"역사 → 역사적인 = \\"historical\\". Modifier form 적인 N.","example_in_sentence":"역사적인 건물들"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~께(서) (honorific dative/subject)","exp":"honorific marker for elders. (Regex false-positive on 함께 here.)","example_in_sentence":""},{"type":"grammar","label":"~과/와 (with/and)","exp":"formal \\"with / and\\". 문화 → 문화와 역사 = \\"culture and history\\".","example_in_sentence":"문화와 역사"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~도 (also)","exp":"inclusive. 역사 → 역사도 = \\"history, too\\".","example_in_sentence":"역사도"}]},{"text":"한국에서도 오래된 건물을 보호하는 것이 중요한 문제예요.","translation":"In Korea too, protecting old buildings is an important issue.","vocab":[{"ko":"보호하다","en":"to protect","note":""},{"ko":"중요하다","en":"to be important","note":""},{"ko":"문제","en":"problem, issue","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~도 (also)","exp":"inclusive. 한국에서 → 한국에서도 = \\"in Korea, also\\".","example_in_sentence":"한국에서도"}]},{"text":"이런 화재를 막기 위한 대책이 필요한 상황이에요.","translation":"It is a situation that requires measures to prevent fires like these.","vocab":[{"ko":"막다","en":"to block, prevent","note":""},{"ko":"대책","en":"countermeasure, plan","note":""},{"ko":"필요하다","en":"to be necessary","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"expression","label":"~기 위한 / ~기 위해","exp":"purpose: \\"in order to / for the sake of\\". 막다 → 막기 위한 대책 = \\"measures (intended) to prevent\\".","example_in_sentence":"막기 위한"}]}],"version":"s5"}', E'[{"ko":"건물","en":"building","note":""},{"ko":"화재","en":"fire (incident)","note":""},{"ko":"발생하다","en":"to occur, break out","note":""},{"ko":"역사적","en":"historical","note":""},{"ko":"가치","en":"value","note":""},{"ko":"오래되다","en":"to be old (of objects)","note":"oft. attributive 오래된"},{"ko":"일어나다","en":"to happen, occur","note":""},{"ko":"지역","en":"area, region","note":""},{"ko":"불타다","en":"to burn (catch fire)","note":""},{"ko":"전문가","en":"expert","note":""},{"ko":"우연","en":"coincidence, chance","note":""},{"ko":"주민","en":"resident","note":""},{"ko":"상황","en":"situation","note":""},{"ko":"걱정하다","en":"to worry","note":""},{"ko":"소방서","en":"fire station","note":""},{"ko":"끄다","en":"to put out, turn off","note":"으-irregular: 끄+어 → 꺼"},{"ko":"원인","en":"cause","note":""},{"ko":"조사하다","en":"to investigate","note":""},{"ko":"경찰","en":"police","note":""},{"ko":"수사","en":"investigation (criminal)","note":""},{"ko":"나서다","en":"to step forward, take part","note":""},{"ko":"사라지다","en":"to disappear","note":""},{"ko":"문화","en":"culture","note":""},{"ko":"없어지다","en":"to vanish, be gone","note":""},{"ko":"보호하다","en":"to protect","note":""},{"ko":"중요하다","en":"to be important","note":""},{"ko":"문제","en":"problem, issue","note":""},{"ko":"막다","en":"to block, prevent","note":""},{"ko":"대책","en":"countermeasure, plan","note":""},{"ko":"필요하다","en":"to be necessary","note":""}]', E'{"patterns":[{"name":"했어요 (하다 past polite)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"하다 verb past polite. 발생하다 → 발생했어요 = \\"occurred\\". 하다 stems contract to 했-.","ex_ko":"미국 캘리포니아주 베이커즈필드의 한 건물에서 1년 동안 23번의 화재가 발생했어요.","ex_en":"In one building in Bakersfield, California, 23 fires broke out over the course of a year."},{"name":"~았/었/였어요 (past polite)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"past polite ending. 하다 stems take the 였- form which contracts to 했-: 발생하다 → 발생했어요.","ex_ko":"미국 캘리포니아주 베이커즈필드의 한 건물에서 1년 동안 23번의 화재가 발생했어요.","ex_en":"In one building in Bakersfield, California, 23 fires broke out over the course of a year."},{"name":"~에서 (location/source)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"location where an action takes place. 건물 → 건물에서 = \\"in/at the building\\".","ex_ko":"미국 캘리포니아주 베이커즈필드의 한 건물에서 1년 동안 23번의 화재가 발생했어요.","ex_en":"In one building in Bakersfield, California, 23 fires broke out over the course of a year."},{"name":"~적 (-ic / -al adjective suffix)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"Sino-Korean noun → adjective. 역사 → 역사적 = \\"historical\\".","ex_ko":"이 건물은 역사적 가치가 있는 오래된 건물이에요.","ex_en":"This building is an old building with historical value."},{"name":"~만 (only)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"limiter \\"only / just\\". 건물에서 → 건물에서만 = \\"only at the building\\".","ex_ko":"이런 일이 이 건물에서만 일어나는 것이 아니에요.","ex_en":"This kind of thing is not happening only in this building."},{"name":"ㄹ 탈락 (ㄹ drops before ㄴ/ㅅ/ㅂ)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"ㄹ-deletion: stem-final ㄹ drops before ㄴ/ㅅ/ㅂ. 살다 → 사니/사세요, 만들다 → 만드세요.","ex_ko":"이런 일이 이 건물에서만 일어나는 것이 아니에요.","ex_en":"This kind of thing is not happening only in this building."},{"name":"~고 있다 (continuous)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"progressive aspect. 걱정하다 → 걱정하고 있다 = \\"is worrying / is worried\\".","ex_ko":"베이커즈필드 지역의 다른 역사적인 건물들도 하나씩 불타고 있어요.","ex_en":"Other historical buildings in the Bakersfield area are also burning one by one."},{"name":"~씩 (each / per)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"distributive. 하나 → 하나씩 = \\"one by one / one each\\".","ex_ko":"베이커즈필드 지역의 다른 역사적인 건물들도 하나씩 불타고 있어요.","ex_en":"Other historical buildings in the Bakersfield area are also burning one by one."},{"name":"~도 (also)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"inclusive. 수도 = 수 + 도 → \\"possibility, too / might also\\". 아닐 수도 있다 = \\"might not be\\".","ex_ko":"베이커즈필드 지역의 다른 역사적인 건물들도 하나씩 불타고 있어요.","ex_en":"Other historical buildings in the Bakersfield area are also burning one by one."},{"name":"~다고 하다 / ~다고 밝히다 / ~다고 강조하다 (indirect declarative + news reporting verbs)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"reported speech. <quote> + 다고 말하다 = \\"say that ~\\". 있다고 말해요 = \\"says that there is / might be\\".","ex_ko":"전문가들은 이것이 우연이 아닐 수도 있다고 말해요.","ex_en":"Experts say that this might not be a coincidence."},{"name":"~하고 (with/and, conv)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"conversational \\"with / and\\". (Here triggered by the ~하고 ending of 걱정하고 — the connector form, not the particle.)","ex_ko":"지역 주민들은 이 상황을 매우 걱정하고 있어요.","ex_en":"Local residents are very worried about this situation."},{"name":"~께(서) (honorific dative/subject)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"honorific marker for elders / superiors. 할아버지 → 할아버지께서. (Here regex false-positive on 함께; the particle is not actually present.)","ex_ko":"경찰도 함께 수사에 나섰어요.","ex_en":"The police also joined the investigation."},{"name":"~(으)면 (if/when)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"conditional. 사라지다 → 사라지면 = \\"if / when (they) disappear\\".","ex_ko":"역사적인 건물들이 사라지면 그 지역의 문화와 역사도 함께 없어져요.","ex_en":"When historical buildings disappear, the culture and history of that area also vanish along with them."},{"name":"~과/와 (with/and)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"formal \\"with / and\\". 문화 → 문화와 역사 = \\"culture and history\\".","ex_ko":"역사적인 건물들이 사라지면 그 지역의 문화와 역사도 함께 없어져요.","ex_en":"When historical buildings disappear, the culture and history of that area also vanish along with them."}]}') ON CONFLICT (article_id) DO UPDATE SET translation = EXCLUDED.translation, vocab = COALESCE(EXCLUDED.vocab, article_cache.vocab), grammar = COALESCE(EXCLUDED.grammar, article_cache.grammar);
INSERT INTO article_cache (article_id, translation, vocab, grammar) VALUES (E'mot918spdjod', E'{"texts":["The Anna\'s hummingbird is a small, beautiful bird. This bird\'s most special feature is its shimmering purple feathers.","But there is a surprising fact. This purple color is not because of pigment. It appears purple because of the very small structures inside the feathers.","On the feathers, there are layers so small that they cannot be seen with the naked eye. These layers act like mirrors and reflect light.","So depending on the angle from which it is viewed, the color changes. This phenomenon is one of the mysterious things that can be seen in nature. So this kind of scientific principle was hidden in the hummingbird\'s beautiful color."],"sentences":[{"text":"안나 벌새(Anna\'s hummingbird)는 작고 아름다운 새예요.","translation":"The Anna\'s hummingbird is a small, beautiful bird.","vocab":[{"ko":"벌새","en":"hummingbird","note":""},{"ko":"아름답다","en":"to be beautiful","note":"vowel-irregular: 아름답+은 → 아름다운"}],"analysis":[]},{"text":"이 새의 가장 특별한 점은 반짝이는 보라색 깃털입니다.","translation":"This bird\'s most special feature is its shimmering purple feathers.","vocab":[{"ko":"특별하다","en":"to be special","note":""},{"ko":"반짝이다","en":"to sparkle, shimmer","note":""},{"ko":"깃털","en":"feather","note":""}],"analysis":[]},{"text":"그런데 놀라운 사실이 있어요.","translation":"But there is a surprising fact.","vocab":[{"ko":"놀랍다","en":"to be surprising","note":"ㅂ-irregular: 놀랍+은 → 놀라운"},{"ko":"사실","en":"fact","note":""}],"analysis":[]},{"text":"이 보라색은 색소 때문이 아니에요.","translation":"This purple color is not because of pigment.","vocab":[{"ko":"보라색","en":"purple (color)","note":""},{"ko":"색소","en":"pigment","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~ 때문에 (because of N)","exp":"because of (noun). 색소 → 색소 때문에 = \\"because of the pigment\\". Negated: 색소 때문이 아니다 = \\"is not because of pigment\\".","example_in_sentence":"색소 때문이"},{"type":"grammar","label":"ㄹ 탈락 (ㄹ drops before ㄴ/ㅅ/ㅂ)","exp":"ㄹ-deletion: stem-final ㄹ drops before ㄴ/ㅅ/ㅂ. 살다 → 사니/사세요, 만들다 → 만드세요, 알다 → 아세요.","example_in_sentence":""}]},{"text":"깃털 안에 있는 아주 작은 구조 때문에 보라색으로 보입니다.","translation":"It appears purple because of the very small structures inside the feathers.","vocab":[{"ko":"구조","en":"structure","note":""},{"ko":"보이다","en":"to be seen, to appear","note":"passive of 보다"}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~ 때문에 (because of N)","exp":"because of (noun). 구조 → 구조 때문에 = \\"because of the structure\\".","example_in_sentence":"구조 때문에"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~(으)로 (means/direction)","exp":"means / direction marker. <noun> + (으)로 = \\"by means of / as / toward\\". 보라색 → 보라색으로 (보이다) = \\"appears as purple\\".","example_in_sentence":"보라색으로"}]},{"text":"깃털에는 눈에 보이지 않을 정도로 작은 층들이 있어요.","translation":"On the feathers, there are layers so small that they cannot be seen with the naked eye.","vocab":[{"ko":"층","en":"layer, floor","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~지요/~죠 (confirming)","exp":"seeking agreement / soft confirmation. 가다 → 가지요/가죠 = \\"you go, right?\\". Note: triggered here by 보이지 in 보이지 않다 sequence.","example_in_sentence":""},{"type":"grammar","label":"~(으)로 (means/direction)","exp":"means / extent marker. <stem> + (으)ㄹ 정도로 = \\"to the extent that\\". 보이지 않을 정도로 = \\"to the extent of not being visible\\".","example_in_sentence":"보이지 않을 정도로"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~(으)ㄹ 정도(이다/로) (to the extent)","exp":"degree marker. 보이지 않다 → 보이지 않을 정도로 = \\"to the point of being invisible\\". <stem> + (으)ㄹ 정도로 sets the extent of an adjective.","example_in_sentence":"보이지 않을 정도로 작은"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~지 않다","exp":"long-form negation. 보이다 → 보이지 않다 = \\"to not be visible\\". 보이지 않을 = \\"that is not visible (modifier)\\".","example_in_sentence":"보이지 않을"}]},{"text":"이 층들이 거울처럼 작용해서 빛을 반사합니다.","translation":"These layers act like mirrors and reflect light.","vocab":[{"ko":"거울","en":"mirror","note":""},{"ko":"작용하다","en":"to act, to function","note":""},{"ko":"빛","en":"light","note":""},{"ko":"반사하다","en":"to reflect","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~아/어서 (cause / sequence)","exp":"reason or sequence connector. 작용하다 → 작용해서 = \\"because (it) acts / and then acts\\". 하다 contracts to 해서.","example_in_sentence":"작용해서"},{"type":"expression","label":"~처럼","exp":"comparison particle: \\"like / as\\". <noun> + 처럼 = \\"like (noun)\\". 거울처럼 = \\"like a mirror\\".","example_in_sentence":"거울처럼"}]},{"text":"그래서 보는 각도에 따라 색깔이 달라져요.","translation":"So depending on the angle from which it is viewed, the color changes.","vocab":[{"ko":"각도","en":"angle","note":""},{"ko":"다르다","en":"to be different","note":"르-irregular: 다르+아 → 달라"},{"ko":"색깔","en":"color","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~에 따라(서) (depending on / as)","exp":"variation / dependence. 각도 → 각도에 따라 = \\"depending on the angle / according to the angle\\".","example_in_sentence":"각도에 따라"},{"type":"grammar","label":"르 불규칙 (르 → ㄹㄹ)","exp":"르-irregular: 다르다 → 달라(요), 모르다 → 몰라, 부르다 → 불러. Here 다르다 + 아져요 → 달라져요 = \\"becomes different\\".","example_in_sentence":"달라져요"},{"type":"expression","label":"~아/어지다 (become)","exp":"change-of-state suffix. 다르다 → 달라지다 = \\"to become different / to change\\". Marks a transition into a state.","example_in_sentence":"달라져요"}]},{"text":"이런 현상은 자연에서 볼 수 있는 신기한 일 중 하나입니다.","translation":"This phenomenon is one of the mysterious things that can be seen in nature.","vocab":[{"ko":"현상","en":"phenomenon","note":""},{"ko":"자연","en":"nature","note":""},{"ko":"신기하다","en":"to be amazing, mysterious","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~(으)ㄹ 수 있다/없다 (ability/possibility)","exp":"ability / possibility. 보다 → 볼 수 있다 = \\"can see / is able to be seen\\". <stem> + (으)ㄹ 수 있다 = \\"can\\"; 없다 = \\"cannot\\".","example_in_sentence":"볼 수 있는"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~에서 (location/source)","exp":"location of an action or source. 자연 → 자연에서 = \\"in nature / from nature\\".","example_in_sentence":"자연에서"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~ 중 하나 (one of)","exp":"\\"one of (a group)\\". 신기한 일 → 신기한 일 중 하나 = \\"one of the mysterious things\\". <group> + 중 하나.","example_in_sentence":"신기한 일 중 하나"}]},{"text":"벌새의 아름다운 색깔에는 이런 과학적 원리가 숨어 있었네요.","translation":"So this kind of scientific principle was hidden in the hummingbird\'s beautiful color.","vocab":[{"ko":"과학적","en":"scientific","note":""},{"ko":"원리","en":"principle","note":""},{"ko":"숨다","en":"to hide","note":""}],"analysis":[{"type":"grammar","label":"~네요 (discovery)","exp":"realization / mild surprise. 있다 → 있었네요 = \\"oh, (it) was\\". Marks discovery: \\"so (it) was, huh\\".","example_in_sentence":"있었네요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~아/어 있다 (resultant state)","exp":"resulting state from a completed action. 숨다 → 숨어 있다 = \\"to remain hidden\\". 숨어 있었다 = \\"was (kept) hidden\\".","example_in_sentence":"숨어 있었네요"},{"type":"grammar","label":"~적 (-ic / -al adjective suffix)","exp":"Sino-Korean noun → adjective. 과학 → 과학적 = \\"scientific\\". Forms: 적이다 / 적인 N / 적으로.","example_in_sentence":"과학적 원리"}]}],"version":"s5"}', E'[{"ko":"벌새","en":"hummingbird","note":""},{"ko":"아름답다","en":"to be beautiful","note":"vowel-irregular: 아름답+은 → 아름다운"},{"ko":"특별하다","en":"to be special","note":""},{"ko":"반짝이다","en":"to sparkle, shimmer","note":""},{"ko":"깃털","en":"feather","note":""},{"ko":"놀랍다","en":"to be surprising","note":"ㅂ-irregular: 놀랍+은 → 놀라운"},{"ko":"사실","en":"fact","note":""},{"ko":"보라색","en":"purple (color)","note":""},{"ko":"색소","en":"pigment","note":""},{"ko":"구조","en":"structure","note":""},{"ko":"보이다","en":"to be seen, to appear","note":"passive of 보다"},{"ko":"층","en":"layer, floor","note":""},{"ko":"거울","en":"mirror","note":""},{"ko":"작용하다","en":"to act, to function","note":""},{"ko":"빛","en":"light","note":""},{"ko":"반사하다","en":"to reflect","note":""},{"ko":"각도","en":"angle","note":""},{"ko":"다르다","en":"to be different","note":"르-irregular: 다르+아 → 달라"},{"ko":"색깔","en":"color","note":""},{"ko":"현상","en":"phenomenon","note":""},{"ko":"자연","en":"nature","note":""},{"ko":"신기하다","en":"to be amazing, mysterious","note":""},{"ko":"과학적","en":"scientific","note":""},{"ko":"원리","en":"principle","note":""},{"ko":"숨다","en":"to hide","note":""}]', E'{"patterns":[{"name":"~ 때문에 (because of N)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"because of (noun). 색소 → 색소 때문에 = \\"because of the pigment\\". Negated: 색소 때문이 아니다 = \\"is not because of pigment\\".","ex_ko":"이 보라색은 색소 때문이 아니에요.","ex_en":"This purple color is not because of pigment."},{"name":"ㄹ 탈락 (ㄹ drops before ㄴ/ㅅ/ㅂ)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"ㄹ-deletion: stem-final ㄹ drops before ㄴ/ㅅ/ㅂ. 살다 → 사니/사세요, 만들다 → 만드세요, 알다 → 아세요.","ex_ko":"이 보라색은 색소 때문이 아니에요.","ex_en":"This purple color is not because of pigment."},{"name":"~(으)로 (means/direction)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"means / extent marker. <stem> + (으)ㄹ 정도로 = \\"to the extent that\\". 보이지 않을 정도로 = \\"to the extent of not being visible\\".","ex_ko":"깃털 안에 있는 아주 작은 구조 때문에 보라색으로 보입니다.","ex_en":"It appears purple because of the very small structures inside the feathers."},{"name":"~지요/~죠 (confirming)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"seeking agreement / soft confirmation. 가다 → 가지요/가죠 = \\"you go, right?\\". Note: triggered here by 보이지 in 보이지 않다 sequence.","ex_ko":"깃털에는 눈에 보이지 않을 정도로 작은 층들이 있어요.","ex_en":"On the feathers, there are layers so small that they cannot be seen with the naked eye."},{"name":"~(으)ㄹ 정도(이다/로) (to the extent)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"degree marker. 보이지 않다 → 보이지 않을 정도로 = \\"to the point of being invisible\\". <stem> + (으)ㄹ 정도로 sets the extent of an adjective.","ex_ko":"깃털에는 눈에 보이지 않을 정도로 작은 층들이 있어요.","ex_en":"On the feathers, there are layers so small that they cannot be seen with the naked eye."},{"name":"~지 않다","level":"Intermediate","exp":"long-form negation. 보이다 → 보이지 않다 = \\"to not be visible\\". 보이지 않을 = \\"that is not visible (modifier)\\".","ex_ko":"깃털에는 눈에 보이지 않을 정도로 작은 층들이 있어요.","ex_en":"On the feathers, there are layers so small that they cannot be seen with the naked eye."},{"name":"~아/어서 (cause / sequence)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"reason or sequence connector. 작용하다 → 작용해서 = \\"because (it) acts / and then acts\\". 하다 contracts to 해서.","ex_ko":"이 층들이 거울처럼 작용해서 빛을 반사합니다.","ex_en":"These layers act like mirrors and reflect light."},{"name":"~에 따라(서) (depending on / as)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"variation / dependence. 각도 → 각도에 따라 = \\"depending on the angle / according to the angle\\".","ex_ko":"그래서 보는 각도에 따라 색깔이 달라져요.","ex_en":"So depending on the angle from which it is viewed, the color changes."},{"name":"르 불규칙 (르 → ㄹㄹ)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"르-irregular: 다르다 → 달라(요), 모르다 → 몰라, 부르다 → 불러. Here 다르다 + 아져요 → 달라져요 = \\"becomes different\\".","ex_ko":"그래서 보는 각도에 따라 색깔이 달라져요.","ex_en":"So depending on the angle from which it is viewed, the color changes."},{"name":"~(으)ㄹ 수 있다/없다 (ability/possibility)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"ability / possibility. 보다 → 볼 수 있다 = \\"can see / is able to be seen\\". <stem> + (으)ㄹ 수 있다 = \\"can\\"; 없다 = \\"cannot\\".","ex_ko":"이런 현상은 자연에서 볼 수 있는 신기한 일 중 하나입니다.","ex_en":"This phenomenon is one of the mysterious things that can be seen in nature."},{"name":"~에서 (location/source)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"location of an action or source. 자연 → 자연에서 = \\"in nature / from nature\\".","ex_ko":"이런 현상은 자연에서 볼 수 있는 신기한 일 중 하나입니다.","ex_en":"This phenomenon is one of the mysterious things that can be seen in nature."},{"name":"~ 중 하나 (one of)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"\\"one of (a group)\\". 신기한 일 → 신기한 일 중 하나 = \\"one of the mysterious things\\". <group> + 중 하나.","ex_ko":"이런 현상은 자연에서 볼 수 있는 신기한 일 중 하나입니다.","ex_en":"This phenomenon is one of the mysterious things that can be seen in nature."},{"name":"~네요 (discovery)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"realization / mild surprise. 있다 → 있었네요 = \\"oh, (it) was\\". Marks discovery: \\"so (it) was, huh\\".","ex_ko":"벌새의 아름다운 색깔에는 이런 과학적 원리가 숨어 있었네요.","ex_en":"So this kind of scientific principle was hidden in the hummingbird\'s beautiful color."},{"name":"~아/어 있다 (resultant state)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"resulting state from a completed action. 숨다 → 숨어 있다 = \\"to remain hidden\\". 숨어 있었다 = \\"was (kept) hidden\\".","ex_ko":"벌새의 아름다운 색깔에는 이런 과학적 원리가 숨어 있었네요.","ex_en":"So this kind of scientific principle was hidden in the hummingbird\'s beautiful color."},{"name":"~적 (-ic / -al adjective suffix)","level":"Intermediate","exp":"Sino-Korean noun → adjective. 과학 → 과학적 = \\"scientific\\". Forms: 적이다 / 적인 N / 적으로.","ex_ko":"벌새의 아름다운 색깔에는 이런 과학적 원리가 숨어 있었네요.","ex_en":"So this kind of scientific principle was hidden in the hummingbird\'s beautiful color."}]}') ON CONFLICT (article_id) DO UPDATE SET translation = EXCLUDED.translation, vocab = COALESCE(EXCLUDED.vocab, article_cache.vocab), grammar = COALESCE(EXCLUDED.grammar, article_cache.grammar);
